-- title:
--   One-sided pool over R[1/f] from level polynomials
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero $N_0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, a level model package $\mathfrak P :$ `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN` for the structure map `toBase N₀ q` $: X(N_0,q) \to \operatorname{Spec}(R_q)$, and $f \in R_q$; write $L =$ `Localization.Away f` and $A =$ `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` for the finite-$j$ chart subalgebra of the modular function field of level $N_0q$. Let $v \in A$ satisfy the dictionary hypothesis: for every algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $q$, every ring map $\mathrm{to}\kappa : R_q \to \kappa$, every point $y$ of the fibre `pullback (toBase N₀ q) (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom toκ))` and every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $A$ with $v \notin \mathfrak q$ whose image under `IgusaScheme.ιFin (N₀ * q) q` is the first projection of $y$, the point $y$ lies in the range of $(\mathfrak P.\mathrm{comp}\,\kappa\,\mathrm{to}\kappa\,0)$ and not in that of $(\mathfrak P.\mathrm{comp}\,\kappa\,\mathrm{to}\kappa\,1)$. Let $b, M$ be naturals, $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,M \to \mathbb Z[X]$ monic polynomials and $rk : \mathrm{Fin}\,M \to \mathbb N$ such that each quotient $A/(g_i(v))$ (the ideal generated by `Polynomial.aeval v (g i)`) is a finite, étale and free $R_q$-module of rank $rk_i$ with $1 \le rk_i \le b$, such that the ideals $(g_i(v))$ are pairwise comaximal, $(g_i(v)) + (g_j(\mathfrak P.\mathrm{theta}\,v)) = \top$ for all $i,j$, and $(g_i(v)) + (v) = \top$ for all $i$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a commutative ring $R'$, an $R_q$-algebra and $L$-algebra structure on $R'$ forming a scalar tower, with $R'$ finite, étale and faithfully flat over $L$; of commutative rings $B_i$ ($i < M$), finite étale $L$-algebras; of degrees $\deg_i$ with $1 \le \deg_i \le b$; of $R'$-algebra isomorphisms $R' \otimes_L B_i \simeq (\mathrm{Fin}\,\deg_i \to R')$; and of morphisms $z_i : \operatorname{Spec} B_i \to \mathcal X_L :=$ `pullback (toBase N₀ q) (specMap (R q) L)`, each a closed immersion, such that: $z_i$ followed by the base-changed structure map `baseChange (R q) (toBase N₀ q) L` is `specMap L (B i)`, so $z_i$ is a morphism over $L$; the set-theoretic range of $z_i$ lies in the preimage under the first projection of the open $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$; the ranges of $z_i$ and $z_j$ are disjoint for $i \ne j$; for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every $s : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every $i$, the preimage of the range of $z_i$ in the geometric fibre `pullback (baseChange (R q) (toBase N₀ q) L) s` is contained in the connected component, inside the preimage of $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$ there, of the point obtained by evaluating `sectionFibrePoint (sectionBaseChange L 𝔓.εinf) s` at the closed point of $k$; the range of each $z_i$ is disjoint from the ranges of the base-changed sections `sectionBaseChange L 𝔓.εinf` and `sectionBaseChange L 𝔓.εzero`; and for all $i,j$ the range of $z_i$ is disjoint from the range of $z_j$ followed by `curveChange 𝔓.w.hom 𝔓.w_over (specMap (R q) L)`.
--
--   This supplies the geometric half of the pool of closed finite étale multisections in the $\infty$-part of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over $R_q[1/f]$: the multisections are cut out on the finite-$j$ chart by values $g_i(v)$ of monic integral polynomials at an element $v$ whose vanishing locus controls the characteristic-$q$ crossings, and the comaximality hypotheses yield disjointness from one another, from the two cusp sections and from the Atkin–Lehner translates. It is the input to the two-sided pool constructions `exists_twoSidedPool_smoothLocus_closedPrime_two`, `exists_twoSidedPool_smoothLocus_closedPrime_three` and `exists_twoSidedPool_smoothLocus_closedPrime_of_five_le`.
-- source:
